      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A1"],
      "reason": "A1 restates the objective and lists obvious alternatives (none, targeted, niche). It does not separate the objective from the suggested solution. Two of the 'targeted expansion' examples (industrial hearing protection, industrial workers) are not consumer propositions. The constraints in A1 are also unsound. 'No expansion into new product lines or markets' contradicts the question itself. 'No financial data available for Hellberg Safety' is false, because hlb-owner reports net sales of SEK 66 m in 2017. The framing also says Hellberg makes 'face protection', but no source excerpt mentions face protection; hlb-head refers to head protection. No missed option is found and no false premise is corrected."
    },
    "causal_mechanism": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A4"],
      "reason": "T1 in A4 offers a status-quo rationale: investment would divert resources, and existing products are 'already well-positioned'. It names a benefit to management and shareholders. It does not explain which customers would or would not change behaviour, or why. 'Already well-positioned in the market' has no supporting source. hlb-head is a company aspiration ('aims to'), not an observation of market position."
    },
    "distinct_theories": {
      "status": "scored",
